# What a play script looks like. Kept as an example rather than as a session:
# every real plan in this directory is named for the day it was played, and is
# the thing an issue points at so a later session can re-run it.
#
#   npm run playbot -- playtest/plans/example.play --view 1280x800 --out /tmp/x
#
# The invite hash lands on the roster with a fight already chosen, which is the
# short way to a particular boss. Walking there from the front page is the long
# way, and both are worth sessions: the long way is the one a player takes.
open #b=gorged&s=25&h=1

# Always list the controls before pressing one. The labels come from the game's
# own hit tests, so a label that is missing here is missing on the screen.
targets
ui
tap class:shaman:elemental
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state

# `flee` is a hypothesis about a player: the one who runs from everything. If
# this ends the same way `good` does, the fight is not asking anything.
shot opening
play flee 240
shot ending

# What the fight said about itself, and what is on the glass now the pull is
# over -- the outcome overlay has its own controls and they are worth listing.
says
targets
ui
